---
// Section 03 (hubstep case study) — the "from / to" reframing of the
// core question. Horizontal before -> after comparison on desktop: a
// quiet "before" card and a more prominent "after" card, both rounded
// pill-like boxes with no left accent line — the "after" card reads as
// more important through its tinted background alone, not bold type or
// a border, so hierarchy stays legible even at normal text weight.
---

<div class="cs">
	<p class="cs__lead">The challenge was shifting from:</p>

	<div class="cs__comparison">
		<div class="cs__card cs__card--before">
			<p class="cs__quote cs__quote--before">“How do we build the SFA?”</p>
		</div>

		<div class="cs__arrow" aria-hidden="true">
			<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
				<path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" />
			</svg>
		</div>

		<div class="cs__card cs__card--after">
			<p class="cs__quote cs__quote--after">
				“How do we make the growing product work as one coherent sales experience?”
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.cs {
		max-width: none;
	}

	.cs__lead {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.cs__comparison {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1.2fr;
		align-items: stretch;
		gap: var(--space-3);
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
	}

	.cs__card {
		padding: var(--space-4);
		border-radius: 40px;
		background: #fafafa;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.cs__quote {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 1.125rem;
	}

	.cs__quote--before {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.cs__card--after {
		background: rgba(10, 126, 113, 0.06);
	}

	.cs__quote--after {
		font-style: normal;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.cs__arrow {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		flex: none;
	}

	.cs__arrow svg {
		width: 20px;
		height: 20px;
	}

	@container (max-width: 640px) {
		.cs__comparison {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			justify-items: stretch;
		}

		.cs__arrow {
			transform: rotate(90deg);
			padding: var(--space-1) 0;
		}
	}
</style>
